  "text": "A plain chat window forgets everything the moment you close it. Claude, Codex, any of them. New tab, blank page, and you're explaining yourself all over again. This is the opposite of that. Every conversation is here, filed by the kind of work it was. Video, images, and design, pages and funnels, planning, open one and pick up mid-sentence. And it isn't only storage. Every correction you make in one of these becomes a rule. Tell it once that you never want a particular word used, and tomorrow it's gone for good. You never say it twice.",
